WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:32.200
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:32.470 --> 00:39.477
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:41.146 --> 00:43.648
‎I found out who ordered ‎Choi Jeong-yo's abduction.

4
01:22.437 --> 01:23.396
‎Hello, Mr. Kang.

5
01:24.230 --> 01:26.107
‎Where did you get this photo?

6
01:26.191 --> 01:28.443
‎Are you positive? ‎Is this information accurate?

7
01:28.526 --> 01:30.320
‎Yes, I'm positive.

8
01:30.945 --> 01:32.739
‎I got my hands on the secret footage

9
01:32.822 --> 01:34.866
‎that the local middlemen had taken ‎just in case.

10
01:34.949 --> 01:36.367
‎And I got their firsthand accounts.

11
01:36.451 --> 01:38.578
‎That can't be right. ‎There's been a mistake.

12
01:39.954 --> 01:41.205
‎The news clearly stated

13
01:41.789 --> 01:43.458
‎that terrorists were behind it.

14
01:43.541 --> 01:45.627
‎They emailed the competition committee ‎demanding a ransom--

15
01:45.710 --> 01:48.713
‎That's a common tactic used ‎to ‎cause ‎confusion.

16
01:51.299 --> 01:52.258
‎Are you all right?

17
01:54.302 --> 01:56.179
‎So what were their orders?

18
01:57.597 --> 01:58.514
‎Were they told

19
01:59.807 --> 02:01.267
‎to kill him?

20
02:04.729 --> 02:06.022
‎No.

21
02:06.105 --> 02:08.066
‎The order was to hold him ‎and release him later.

22
02:09.275 --> 02:10.401
‎But things went sideways.

23
02:11.611 --> 02:12.612
‎The person in the photo…

24
02:14.364 --> 02:15.531
‎is your mother, right?

25
02:32.048 --> 02:36.469
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

26
02:37.178 --> 02:39.055
‎EPISODE 9

27
03:03.997 --> 03:07.667
‎Wasn't Pi-o absolutely amazing today?

28
03:07.750 --> 03:09.168
‎Totally.

29
03:09.252 --> 03:11.796
‎He absolutely killed it.

30
03:11.879 --> 03:13.923
‎I knew he could do it.

31
03:14.007 --> 03:15.758
‎That slump he was in?

32
03:15.842 --> 03:17.635
‎I knew he'd get over it before long.

33
03:18.386 --> 03:20.013
‎Because Pi-o is

34
03:20.638 --> 03:24.017
‎a special gift sent to me from God.

35
03:24.100 --> 03:25.560
‎Agreed.

36
03:25.643 --> 03:27.854
‎To your son, Pi-o Kang.

37
03:28.354 --> 03:32.275
‎He's totally a gift from the heavens.

38
03:36.612 --> 03:40.783
‎From the moment I discovered his talent,

39
03:41.326 --> 03:45.496
‎I never once doubted ‎he'd become a great pianist.

40
03:45.580 --> 03:47.290
‎I clearly saw it coming.

41
03:48.082 --> 03:49.917
‎So I did everything I could.

42
03:50.668 --> 03:53.004
‎I did whatever it took for Pi-o.

43
03:53.087 --> 03:56.799
‎That's what made Pi-o who he is today.

44
03:57.342 --> 03:58.176
‎Don't you agree?

45
03:58.259 --> 03:59.344
‎I do.

46
03:59.844 --> 04:02.764
‎You're really amazing.

47
04:04.098 --> 04:05.600
‎But please don't forget

48
04:05.683 --> 04:09.729
‎that we set the stage for them ‎at the right moment.

49
04:09.812 --> 04:12.357
‎Pairing two people ‎with that kind of chemistry

50
04:12.440 --> 04:14.984
‎is what created that magic, right?

51
04:16.652 --> 04:18.029
‎You're right.

52
04:18.112 --> 04:21.741
‎They certainly have a special chemistry.

53
04:40.009 --> 04:41.302
‎Gosh, you scared me.

54
04:43.763 --> 04:44.764
‎Pi-o.

55
04:45.306 --> 04:46.933
‎Is the after-party already over?

56
04:49.310 --> 04:50.311
‎Why are you here?

57
04:52.188 --> 04:53.940
‎Did you stay up to see me?

58
04:56.734 --> 04:58.694
‎I was so happy today.

59
04:59.987 --> 05:03.699
‎I knew you would do a phenomenal job.

60
05:04.283 --> 05:07.120
‎Tell everyone who said you hit a slump ‎to show their faces.

61
05:17.505 --> 05:18.423
‎What's wrong?

62
05:20.174 --> 05:21.801
‎Why did you do it, Mom?

63
05:22.385 --> 05:23.594
‎What do you mean?

64
05:23.678 --> 05:26.305
‎Why did you hire someone ‎to abduct Jeong-yo?

65
05:28.683 --> 05:30.476
‎I don't know what you're talking about.

66
05:35.356 --> 05:37.400
‎How could someone do that ‎to another person?

67
05:37.984 --> 05:40.278
‎How could you commit a crime like that?

68
05:40.361 --> 05:42.029
‎I knew you doubted me,

69
05:42.113 --> 05:44.407
‎but what on earth were you thinking?

70
05:46.701 --> 05:49.078
‎I have no idea what you're saying.

71
05:49.162 --> 05:50.830
‎Hire? Abduct?

72
05:51.998 --> 05:54.375
‎How could you accuse me ‎of something so horrifying?

73
06:01.841 --> 06:02.717
‎Where…

74
06:04.719 --> 06:05.970
‎Where did you get this photo?

75
06:06.053 --> 06:07.138
‎That's not the point.

76
06:07.221 --> 06:08.514
‎I asked you a question!

77
06:08.598 --> 06:11.726
‎I got it from the middlemen ‎you hired for the abduction.

78
06:11.809 --> 06:12.685
‎So?

79
06:13.978 --> 06:15.313
‎Will you still deny it?

80
06:29.202 --> 06:30.036
‎You're right.

81
06:31.329 --> 06:32.538
‎I ordered the abduction.

82
06:35.458 --> 06:38.002
‎It was the finals, ‎and you hurt your finger.

83
06:39.378 --> 06:40.463
‎I couldn't think straight.

84
06:41.589 --> 06:44.217
‎I devoted my entire life ‎to seeing you win,

85
06:44.300 --> 06:46.385
‎but you said you'd quit if you didn't.

86
06:46.469 --> 06:47.970
‎It drove me insane.

87
06:48.471 --> 06:49.430
‎But Pi-o,

88
06:50.348 --> 06:51.766
‎I need you to know this.

89
06:53.017 --> 06:55.603
‎I had no intention of killing him.

90
06:55.686 --> 06:58.397
‎I told them to keep him for a bit ‎and let him go.

91
06:58.981 --> 07:01.025
‎I thought about everything ‎from turning myself in

92
07:01.108 --> 07:02.276
‎to coming clean to you.

93
07:02.360 --> 07:03.194
‎But then…

94
07:05.947 --> 07:08.241
‎Then you won first place ‎at the competition.

95
07:11.327 --> 07:13.663
‎I couldn't lay that disgrace on you.

96
07:14.163 --> 07:16.165
‎Not after everything ‎you went through to earn it.

97
07:18.042 --> 07:19.043
‎You understand

98
07:19.919 --> 07:21.504
‎why I had to do it, right?

99
07:23.839 --> 07:25.508
‎I just wanted the best for you.

100
07:26.300 --> 07:27.218
‎It was for you.

101
07:27.301 --> 07:29.512
‎Stop talking nonsense!

102
07:29.595 --> 07:33.349
‎Did you think about ‎how disgraceful it'd be to win like that?

103
07:33.432 --> 07:34.892
‎Because of that accident,

104
07:34.976 --> 07:37.395
‎Jeong-yo can't play the piano anymore ‎and lost his memories!

105
07:37.478 --> 07:39.730
‎It was hard for me too!

106
07:40.898 --> 07:43.067
‎I thought I had lost my mind ‎and regretted it so much.

107
07:43.734 --> 07:46.279
‎I haven't slept peacefully ‎since that happened.

108
07:46.362 --> 07:47.238
‎But…

109
07:49.156 --> 07:50.700
‎what can we do about it now?

110
07:51.450 --> 07:52.910
‎If the truth comes out,

111
07:53.536 --> 07:56.163
‎both of our lives will be over.

112
07:56.747 --> 07:58.249
‎How could I possibly live like that?

113
07:58.332 --> 08:01.127
‎People will point fingers at me, ‎saying I ruined your life.

114
08:02.169 --> 08:04.297
‎I wouldn't last a single day of that.

115
08:05.423 --> 08:06.841
‎If you commit a crime,

116
08:06.924 --> 08:08.301
‎you should be punished.

117
08:08.384 --> 08:09.802
‎That goes for both of us.

118
08:10.845 --> 08:11.971
‎Let's go.

119
08:12.054 --> 08:13.889
‎We'll confess to Jeong-yo ‎and ask for his forgiveness.

120
08:13.973 --> 08:15.600
‎No, I won't go!

121
08:17.059 --> 08:18.728
‎Jeong-yo didn't die after all,

122
08:19.770 --> 08:20.771
‎and now…

123
08:21.689 --> 08:23.190
‎now we're back to where we started.

124
08:29.947 --> 08:30.823
‎Pi-o.

125
08:31.449 --> 08:33.159
‎As long as we bury this secret,

126
08:33.826 --> 08:36.162
‎we can go on living like nothing happened.

127
08:36.245 --> 08:37.246
‎So please…

128
08:39.498 --> 08:41.083
‎Do you hear yourself?

129
08:41.167 --> 08:42.835
‎That won't make the crime just disappear.

130
08:43.753 --> 08:44.837
‎Mom.

131
08:45.421 --> 08:48.132
‎Do you really want to hit rock bottom?

132
08:49.342 --> 08:50.509
‎Come on.

133
08:50.593 --> 08:52.595
‎Let's go and tell him everything.

134
08:52.678 --> 08:54.639
‎No!

135
08:57.683 --> 08:58.976
‎I'd rather die

136
09:00.311 --> 09:01.937
‎than let anyone know about this.

137
09:02.938 --> 09:03.814
‎Are you…

138
09:04.607 --> 09:06.525
‎willing to let me die like this?

139
10:52.798 --> 10:54.800
‎What brings you here at this hour?

140
11:03.142 --> 11:05.269
‎What is this about? Why are you stalling?

141
11:05.352 --> 11:06.562
‎Go on, tell me.

142
11:12.568 --> 11:13.694
‎You don't look well.

143
11:14.820 --> 11:16.238
‎Are you hiding something from me?

144
11:24.455 --> 11:25.289
‎Yes.

145
11:26.749 --> 11:28.959
‎So I'm here to ask for your forgiveness.

146
11:32.254 --> 11:34.798
‎Nine years ago ‎at the Harmonie International Competition…

147
11:37.760 --> 11:39.470
‎I'd rather die

148
11:40.095 --> 11:41.764
‎than let anyone know about this.

149
11:41.847 --> 11:42.765
‎Are you…

150
11:43.641 --> 11:46.852
‎willing to let me die like this?

151
11:56.070 --> 11:58.072
‎I was able to win the competition

152
11:59.573 --> 12:01.158
‎because of your sheet music.

153
12:02.409 --> 12:04.912
‎I'd lost the sheet music for the set piece ‎at the chapel,

154
12:04.995 --> 12:06.205
‎so I was going to withdraw.

155
12:07.331 --> 12:09.333
‎But you lent me yours.

156
12:10.292 --> 12:12.127
‎I only managed to play so well

157
12:12.753 --> 12:14.713
‎thanks to the notes you left.

158
12:16.131 --> 12:17.466
‎So where I stand right now…

159
12:20.636 --> 12:21.595
‎belongs to you.

160
12:23.180 --> 12:25.432
‎I didn't have the courage ‎to tell you the truth before.

161
12:30.604 --> 12:31.438
‎I'm sorry.

162
12:49.748 --> 12:50.583
‎That's it?

163
12:52.543 --> 12:54.003
‎That's what you wanted to tell me?

164
12:55.296 --> 12:57.089
‎I don't quite understand.

165
12:57.172 --> 12:58.591
‎All this over sheet music?

166
12:59.592 --> 13:01.051
‎Interpreting it is one thing.

167
13:02.052 --> 13:03.846
‎But how you play it is another matter.

168
13:05.806 --> 13:06.765
‎I watched

169
13:08.058 --> 13:09.685
‎a video of your competition performance.

170
13:10.769 --> 13:13.397
‎You had a distinct style ‎that went beyond interpretation.

171
13:14.356 --> 13:16.567
‎Anyway, I don't care about ‎things like that.

172
13:18.235 --> 13:19.194
‎Come on.

173
13:21.030 --> 13:24.325
‎You had me scared ‎because you looked so serious.

174
14:02.696 --> 14:05.532
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

175
14:22.966 --> 14:26.470
‎MOM

176
14:31.016 --> 14:32.309
‎The call cannot be connected.

177
14:32.393 --> 14:35.437
‎You will be connected to voicemail ‎after the beep,

178
14:35.521 --> 14:36.647
‎and call charges will apply.

179
14:53.330 --> 14:54.832
‎Where were you?

180
14:59.878 --> 15:00.879
‎Pi-o.

181
15:02.464 --> 15:03.549
‎Did you tell him?

182
15:04.675 --> 15:05.718
‎You told him?

183
15:19.565 --> 15:20.482
‎Go inside.

184
15:34.079 --> 15:35.247
‎What is it?

185
15:36.999 --> 15:38.959
‎I didn't get a chance ‎to tell you something.

186
15:40.169 --> 15:41.295
‎Can I come in?

187
15:49.011 --> 15:50.387
‎This is a nice practice room.

188
15:52.222 --> 15:53.640
‎You get great sunlight.

189
15:54.266 --> 15:57.728
‎The music would just play itself ‎in a room like this.

190
15:58.520 --> 15:59.772
‎What did you want to tell me?

191
16:00.522 --> 16:01.356
‎Right.

192
16:08.781 --> 16:09.656
‎What's this?

193
16:09.740 --> 16:11.658
‎It's the piano concerto I composed.

194
16:12.618 --> 16:14.203
‎It took me five years to finish.

195
16:14.828 --> 16:17.206
‎I felt it was time ‎to share this with the world,

196
16:17.289 --> 16:19.708
‎so I've been looking for ‎a soloist to play it.

197
16:20.667 --> 16:21.585
‎Mr. Kang.

198
16:23.087 --> 16:24.588
‎Please be the first to play this.

199
16:27.091 --> 16:28.217
‎I can't.

200
16:29.176 --> 16:30.052
‎Why not?

201
16:30.135 --> 16:31.804
‎I already told you. I…

202
16:34.556 --> 16:36.725
‎I have no right to play that.

203
16:37.309 --> 16:38.894
‎And I already told you.

204
16:39.728 --> 16:43.023
‎I merely provided the interpretation. ‎You won first place on your own merits.

205
16:44.399 --> 16:47.027
‎At least check it out ‎before you shut me down.

206
16:47.945 --> 16:49.446
‎You haven't even looked at it.

207
17:44.918 --> 17:45.919
‎Just as I thought.

208
17:46.795 --> 17:47.713
‎I can't do it.

209
17:47.796 --> 17:50.132
‎Why not? You don't like the piece?

210
17:50.716 --> 17:52.843
‎No, the piece is beautiful.

211
17:53.719 --> 17:56.471
‎I can tell how much effort ‎you put into it.

212
17:57.598 --> 17:59.766
‎Everyone will be stunned ‎when it comes out.

213
17:59.850 --> 18:01.226
‎Then why won't you do it?

214
18:02.853 --> 18:03.770
‎Just…

215
18:05.647 --> 18:08.650
‎Just find someone else.

216
18:09.776 --> 18:11.486
‎I just told you.

217
18:14.948 --> 18:17.826
‎I've looked everywhere, ‎and you're the one I want.

218
18:18.952 --> 18:21.288
‎I don't need just any pianist.

219
18:21.371 --> 18:25.250
‎I need someone as dedicated as I am ‎who will pour their soul into it.

220
18:26.168 --> 18:28.629
‎Our recent performance ‎made me even more certain.

221
18:28.712 --> 18:31.173
‎The only person ‎who would give it their all

222
18:31.924 --> 18:33.383
‎is you, Mr. Kang.

223
18:35.802 --> 18:37.512
‎What if we look at it this way?

224
18:40.057 --> 18:42.184
‎If you've been ‎torturing yourself with guilt,

225
18:43.602 --> 18:46.605
‎use this as an opportunity ‎to make it up to me.

226
18:47.856 --> 18:49.107
‎Still not interested?

227
18:51.944 --> 18:54.321
‎If you won't do it, ‎I won't release the piece.

228
18:55.781 --> 18:56.865
‎So choose your answer wisely.

229
18:58.450 --> 19:00.327
‎I'm going to wait until you say yes.

230
19:08.543 --> 19:09.586
‎I'll be off then.

231
19:11.338 --> 19:12.923
‎I'll be looking forward to good news.

232
19:31.858 --> 19:33.318
‎What did he mean by that?

233
19:33.402 --> 19:34.778
‎Do what together?

234
19:34.861 --> 19:36.154
‎Were you eavesdropping?

235
19:38.991 --> 19:40.575
‎What did he mean by you feeling guilty?

236
19:40.659 --> 19:42.369
‎How much did you tell him?

237
19:42.911 --> 19:45.163
‎I didn't tell him about you, so just stop.

238
19:45.706 --> 19:47.624
‎Stay out of my business.

239
19:53.046 --> 19:54.214
‎You asked me before

240
19:55.048 --> 19:57.175
‎why I'm conducting instead of playing.

241
19:57.759 --> 19:58.802
‎Nine years ago,

242
19:59.845 --> 20:01.680
‎I got shot in my right shoulder.

243
20:02.639 --> 20:04.308
‎It caused nerve damage in my fingers.

244
20:04.391 --> 20:07.060
‎I can get through daily life, ‎but I can't play anymore.

245
20:08.812 --> 20:11.273
‎Take away music from a musician, ‎and he's left with hell.

246
20:12.649 --> 20:13.734
‎But a slump…

247
20:15.319 --> 20:17.195
‎is something you can work your way out of.

248
20:18.447 --> 20:19.489
‎That's not the case for me.

249
20:20.741 --> 20:22.617
‎I'm actually envious of you.

250
20:29.041 --> 20:31.001
‎If you've been ‎torturing yourself with guilt,

251
20:32.544 --> 20:35.380
‎use this as an opportunity ‎to make it up to me.

252
20:48.185 --> 20:50.145
‎CHOI JEONG-YO: ‎HOW LONG WILL YOU KEEP ME WAITING?

253
20:50.228 --> 20:52.147
‎IF YOU FEEL BAD ABOUT THE PAST, ‎THEN JUST DO IT.

254
21:28.100 --> 21:29.017
‎I'll do it.

255
21:29.976 --> 21:32.312
‎If that's what you want, ‎I'll give it my best.

256
21:34.314 --> 21:35.899
‎But if you're not satisfied…

257
21:37.651 --> 21:39.444
‎you can replace me anytime.

258
21:39.528 --> 21:41.363
‎I genuinely want to make an effort…

259
21:44.658 --> 21:45.951
‎for your sake.

260
21:51.081 --> 21:53.083
‎You composed this?

261
21:53.583 --> 21:54.668
‎Yes, sir.

262
21:56.837 --> 21:58.839
‎It's not bad for your first piece.

263
22:01.216 --> 22:02.384
‎The only thing is…

264
22:03.093 --> 22:06.221
‎Were you thinking of someone ‎when you composed this?

265
22:07.305 --> 22:08.306
‎How strange.

266
22:09.224 --> 22:12.644
‎Why do I hear the composer's narrative ‎before the music itself?

267
22:16.064 --> 22:16.982
‎I'm not sure.

268
22:18.316 --> 22:20.944
‎I just tried to put ‎my true feelings into it.

269
22:24.823 --> 22:25.991
‎So,

270
22:26.074 --> 22:28.994
‎why did you show this to me?

271
22:31.955 --> 22:32.914
‎I was hoping…

272
22:35.542 --> 22:38.712
‎to premiere this piece at the orchestra's ‎80th anniversary festival.

273
22:40.297 --> 22:42.132
‎What do you think of it, Mr. Kang?

274
22:43.175 --> 22:44.009
‎All right.

275
22:45.135 --> 22:46.553
‎Go ahead and do it.

276
22:49.139 --> 22:50.098
‎However,

277
22:50.849 --> 22:54.853
‎I hope the performance ‎can move beyond personal sentiment

278
22:56.354 --> 22:58.607
‎and become a piece ‎that speaks to everyone.

279
22:59.274 --> 23:00.692
‎Can you do that?

280
23:01.985 --> 23:02.903
‎Yes, sir.

281
23:03.987 --> 23:06.531
‎Is there a soloist you have in mind?

282
23:07.741 --> 23:09.701
‎Yes, I do.

283
23:12.537 --> 23:13.872
‎Pianist Kang Pi-o.

284
23:18.084 --> 23:19.211
‎Pi-o?

285
23:21.630 --> 23:22.505
‎Really?

286
23:23.215 --> 23:28.011
‎How about a more explosive ‎and powerful pianist?

287
23:28.803 --> 23:31.932
‎I believe he has that kind of potential.

288
23:33.141 --> 23:34.517
‎And I can draw it out of him.

289
23:44.402 --> 23:46.196
‎This is a beautiful piece.

290
23:53.328 --> 23:56.414
‎Pi-o is truly so lucky.

291
24:13.848 --> 24:15.725
‎May I ask you something?

292
24:16.518 --> 24:17.602
‎Yes.

293
24:17.686 --> 24:22.399
‎You seem unusually harsh on Pi-o.

294
24:24.234 --> 24:27.279
‎He's had a lot of success ‎and earned a reputation.

295
24:27.904 --> 24:29.489
‎Isn't it time to acknowledge him?

296
24:30.323 --> 24:31.658
‎So why do you still--

297
24:31.741 --> 24:33.535
‎He takes after me.

298
24:35.745 --> 24:37.372
‎He'll push himself to the limit…

299
24:40.208 --> 24:42.961
‎then choose to self-destruct ‎if it doesn't work out.

300
24:44.421 --> 24:45.547
‎You see,

301
24:45.630 --> 24:50.343
‎art is a nasty beast that won't rest ‎until it drains you dry.

302
24:56.016 --> 24:58.476
‎It does that even to talented musicians.

303
25:01.021 --> 25:02.022
‎Just imagine…

304
25:04.649 --> 25:06.651
‎what it would do to those who aren't.

305
25:19.998 --> 25:21.916
‎Goodness, you're amazing.

306
25:24.002 --> 25:24.961
‎Jeong-yo.

307
25:25.712 --> 25:28.590
‎In addition to premiering this piece,

308
25:28.673 --> 25:31.593
‎how about releasing an album ‎before the 80th anniversary festival?

309
25:31.676 --> 25:33.595
‎-An album? ‎-Yeah.

310
25:33.678 --> 25:36.306
‎If you release an album,

311
25:36.389 --> 25:39.434
‎it'll establish the two of you as a brand, ‎like I suggested before.

312
25:40.060 --> 25:43.605
‎It'll give the 80th anniversary festival ‎a huge promotional boost as well.

313
25:44.230 --> 25:46.024
‎That's a great idea.

314
25:46.983 --> 25:48.610
‎What do you think, Jeong-yo?

315
25:49.652 --> 25:52.947
‎Well, as long as the pianist agrees…

316
25:58.995 --> 25:59.996
‎No, Pi-o.

317
26:01.998 --> 26:03.291
‎Why would you do this?

318
26:03.375 --> 26:05.168
‎You should be steering clear of him.

319
26:05.251 --> 26:07.170
‎Why do you keep ‎involving yourself with him?

320
26:07.253 --> 26:09.005
‎Why are you playing with fire?

321
26:09.089 --> 26:11.257
‎You're only worried about getting caught.

322
26:11.341 --> 26:13.093
‎You feel no guilt toward Jeong-yo, do you?

323
26:14.844 --> 26:18.056
‎The only way I can make it up to him ‎is to perform well.

324
26:19.682 --> 26:21.518
‎What if he's up to something?

325
26:22.102 --> 26:24.604
‎I'm terrified ‎he's getting in your way on purpose.

326
26:27.190 --> 26:28.733
‎Even if that's true, it can't be helped.

327
26:30.193 --> 26:32.779
‎If I can be the fuel for his fire,

328
26:33.655 --> 26:34.864
‎I'll do it.

329
26:42.580 --> 26:43.623
‎Eighty years ago,

330
26:43.706 --> 26:47.961
‎through the scars of war, ‎music kept us breathing.

331
26:48.044 --> 26:49.212
‎PRESS CONFERENCE ‎LEGACY &amp; LEAP

332
26:49.295 --> 26:52.424
‎From a quiet, humble beginning, ‎the Hankook Symphony now stands

333
26:52.507 --> 26:55.593
‎as a globally recognized name ‎in the world of music.

334
26:55.677 --> 26:56.719
‎3. A MESSAGE FROM THE FUTURE

335
26:56.803 --> 27:00.140
‎This festival will celebrate that journey

336
27:00.223 --> 27:03.768
‎while laying the groundwork ‎for the next generation…

337
27:03.852 --> 27:05.645
‎Working with Maestro Kang

338
27:06.354 --> 27:08.022
‎always excites me.

339
27:08.606 --> 27:13.820
‎The way he continues to explore music ‎and isn't afraid to break the mold

340
27:14.529 --> 27:16.489
‎keeps me on my toes.

341
27:17.073 --> 27:19.451
‎I chose Pianist Kang Pi-o

342
27:19.534 --> 27:23.246
‎because beneath his refined ‎and disciplined performance

343
27:23.329 --> 27:24.914
‎lies a burning passion.

344
27:25.623 --> 27:27.750
‎As we all know, the finest performance

345
27:28.376 --> 27:31.629
‎comes from a cool head ‎and a passionate heart.

346
27:31.713 --> 27:33.548
‎I am fully committed

347
27:34.883 --> 27:36.342
‎to delivering a premiere

348
27:37.177 --> 27:38.261
‎worthy of the composer.

349
27:51.566 --> 27:52.400
‎Jeong-yo.

350
27:53.860 --> 27:55.320
‎I'm a little upset.

351
27:56.946 --> 27:58.573
‎I saw the piece you composed.

352
27:58.656 --> 28:01.242
‎I'm pretty confident I can play it well.

353
28:02.035 --> 28:05.580
‎But you didn't even consider me ‎and went straight to your friend.

354
28:06.915 --> 28:08.208
‎I'm sorry.

355
28:08.291 --> 28:09.709
‎But I felt that the right person

356
28:10.835 --> 28:12.045
‎would be Mr. Kang here.

357
28:12.670 --> 28:13.505
‎I see.

358
28:14.589 --> 28:15.840
‎Come on, Mr. Do.

359
28:16.966 --> 28:18.885
‎You can't really complain

360
28:18.968 --> 28:21.429
‎when you've been ‎Mr. Kang's favorite for years.

361
28:22.180 --> 28:25.350
‎Just let Pi-o and Jeong-yo ‎love each other in peace.

362
28:25.433 --> 28:27.852
‎Oh, is that how it is?

363
28:30.104 --> 28:33.858
‎Goodness, artists are so possessive ‎when it comes to premieres.

364
28:33.942 --> 28:36.110
‎Jeong-yo, you'll need to step it up

365
28:36.194 --> 28:39.239
‎if you're going to write pieces ‎for the musicians standing in line.

366
28:40.949 --> 28:42.909
‎Anyway, I'm so happy.

367
28:42.992 --> 28:47.372
‎To think my students would turn around ‎and become my competitors…

368
28:47.455 --> 28:49.791
‎Isn't this what all teachers hope for?

369
28:51.376 --> 28:52.377
‎Pi-o.

370
28:53.503 --> 28:55.713
‎Make sure to dominate the stage again

371
28:55.797 --> 28:58.383
‎and keep me on my toes, okay?

372
28:59.425 --> 29:00.343
‎Yes, sir.

373
29:01.761 --> 29:02.595
‎Hyun-soo.

374
29:03.263 --> 29:05.473
‎-Come over here. ‎-Yes, sir.

375
29:08.226 --> 29:11.896
‎Look at that. ‎Mr. Kang still adores Hyun-soo.

376
29:13.314 --> 29:14.858
‎Oh, right.

377
29:16.526 --> 29:18.736
‎Can we touch base while you practice

378
29:18.820 --> 29:22.240
‎and talk about how ‎the piece is coming together?

379
29:22.824 --> 29:24.284
‎Since it's my first piece,

380
29:24.868 --> 29:27.662
‎I'd like us to discuss it ‎as if we're creating it together.

381
29:28.246 --> 29:29.122
‎Of course.

382
29:29.914 --> 29:31.124
‎I'll do that.

383
29:39.382 --> 29:40.466
‎All of them?

384
29:40.550 --> 29:42.218
‎Yeah. All of them.

385
29:43.761 --> 29:47.056
‎Can't you at least accept the invitations ‎to Salzburg and Lucerne?

386
29:47.765 --> 29:49.225
‎I don't want to lose focus.

387
29:50.184 --> 29:51.644
‎Cancel all of my performances.

388
29:52.687 --> 29:54.355
‎And don't accept any new invitations.

389
29:55.815 --> 29:56.649
‎Please.

390
29:58.151 --> 29:59.193
‎Hey, guys.

391
30:01.195 --> 30:04.532
‎Why don't we send everyone off ‎and grab a beer?

392
30:05.575 --> 30:06.784
‎I'm sorry.

393
30:06.868 --> 30:09.370
‎I have something to do, so I need to go.

394
30:09.454 --> 30:12.415
‎Come on, we don't get together ‎like this very often.

395
30:12.498 --> 30:13.666
‎Just stay a bit longer.

396
30:14.876 --> 30:15.835
‎I'm sorry.

397
30:16.628 --> 30:18.254
‎All right then. Get home safe.

398
30:18.338 --> 30:19.297
‎Okay.

399
30:37.357 --> 30:39.859
‎Sorry, guys.

400
30:39.943 --> 30:42.403
‎Something urgent came up. ‎Let's grab a beer next time.

401
30:43.404 --> 30:45.114
‎-Okay, Mr. Do. Good night. ‎-Sorry.

402
30:59.212 --> 31:00.088
‎Ji-hye.

403
31:00.588 --> 31:01.631
‎Kang Ji-hye.

404
31:04.759 --> 31:06.469
‎Pull it together.

405
31:14.018 --> 31:15.061
‎Here.

406
31:19.524 --> 31:20.441
‎Hyun-soo.

407
31:22.860 --> 31:23.695
‎Hyun-soo.

408
31:25.446 --> 31:26.406
‎Hyun-soo.

409
31:28.491 --> 31:29.325
‎Hyun-soo.

410
31:31.661 --> 31:32.829
‎Everyone…

411
31:34.872 --> 31:36.499
‎makes mistakes

412
31:37.500 --> 31:39.836
‎as they go through life, right?

413
31:43.965 --> 31:44.799
‎I know.

414
31:46.718 --> 31:48.886
‎I know I'm a horrible person.

415
31:48.970 --> 31:50.096
‎I really do.

416
31:52.223 --> 31:53.307
‎But I had no choice.

417
31:55.101 --> 31:55.977
‎I had no choice.

418
31:56.060 --> 31:58.396
‎That's enough. Let's get you home, Ji-hye.

419
31:58.479 --> 32:00.314
‎Come on, get up.

420
32:02.692 --> 32:04.277
‎My poor Pi-o…

421
32:06.529 --> 32:08.698
‎My poor, pitiful Pi-o…

422
32:11.159 --> 32:13.327
‎Please save Pi-o.

423
32:14.746 --> 32:17.331
‎Please get Choi Jeong-yo away from Pi-o.

424
32:17.415 --> 32:18.833
‎I'm so scared.

425
32:20.209 --> 32:21.878
‎I'm scared to death.

426
33:07.006 --> 33:09.133
‎I wanted to see you today

427
33:10.760 --> 33:14.263
‎because after the orchestra's ‎80th anniversary performance,

428
33:15.264 --> 33:18.017
‎I'm going to step down ‎as artistic director.

429
33:19.060 --> 33:19.894
‎What?

430
33:20.645 --> 33:21.604
‎I would like my successor…

431
33:22.939 --> 33:25.525
‎to be Choi Jeong-yo.

432
33:27.860 --> 33:29.403
‎What do you think?

433
33:30.029 --> 33:31.572
‎What do you mean?

434
33:36.327 --> 33:38.746
‎I'm against it. It's too soon.

435
33:38.830 --> 33:41.207
‎No, I've done enough.

436
33:41.874 --> 33:44.752
‎For the orchestra to turn a new page,

437
33:46.295 --> 33:48.422
‎it needs fresh talent.

438
33:49.549 --> 33:52.135
‎And I think Jeong-yo is the right person.

439
33:52.218 --> 33:53.094
‎No.

440
33:54.679 --> 33:57.140
‎You can't retire ‎when you're still this healthy.

441
33:58.182 --> 33:59.392
‎Besides,

442
33:59.475 --> 34:02.812
‎I'm only here ‎because I like making music with you.

443
34:03.563 --> 34:04.939
‎You can't do this to me.

444
34:08.776 --> 34:09.610
‎By any chance,

445
34:10.653 --> 34:12.363
‎are you feeling unwell?

446
34:13.281 --> 34:15.074
‎Are you hiding something from me?

447
34:17.618 --> 34:19.620
‎Please tell me.

448
34:20.663 --> 34:21.914
‎It's not like that.

449
34:25.042 --> 34:27.461
‎I'm leaving because there's nothing sadder

450
34:27.545 --> 34:29.255
‎than an old man overstaying his welcome.

451
34:29.839 --> 34:31.132
‎Try to understand.

452
34:40.641 --> 34:43.811
‎MAHLER'S SYMPHONY NO. 5, 4TH MOVEMENT ‎CONDUCTOR: KANG SEUNG-WOON

453
35:07.460 --> 35:08.336
‎Continuing from yesterday…

454
35:09.962 --> 35:12.798
‎Fourth movement, the ‎Adagietto‎.

455
35:13.299 --> 35:15.593
‎All right. Let's begin.

456
35:50.002 --> 35:52.296
‎Don't just play. Put more feeling into it!

457
35:59.887 --> 36:02.348
‎Play the emotion, not just the notes!

458
36:16.028 --> 36:17.405
‎Do you know

459
36:18.406 --> 36:21.784
‎what's missing from our performance?

460
36:23.661 --> 36:25.955
‎You played the notes well.

461
36:26.038 --> 36:27.248
‎But can you make music…

462
36:29.417 --> 36:33.170
‎simply by following the markings ‎on the page?

463
36:34.213 --> 36:35.756
‎You see,

464
36:37.258 --> 36:40.803
‎the ‎Adagietto ‎is a love letter ‎Mahler sent to Alma.

465
36:42.847 --> 36:44.974
‎He loved her so much

466
36:45.057 --> 36:47.351
‎that he wrote her a musical love letter.

467
36:50.354 --> 36:51.522
‎But our performance…

468
36:53.524 --> 36:55.276
‎has none of that love.

469
36:59.280 --> 37:01.490
‎Stop obsessing over the notes,

470
37:01.574 --> 37:04.744
‎understand the emotions, ‎and pour your soul into it.

471
37:06.620 --> 37:08.831
‎The reason I keep nagging…

472
37:11.834 --> 37:15.755
‎is because I want you all ‎to own the music.

473
37:17.465 --> 37:19.050
‎Each and every one of us

474
37:19.800 --> 37:21.552
‎must own the music

475
37:22.136 --> 37:26.265
‎for our energy to resonate ‎and move the audience.

476
37:26.849 --> 37:30.436
‎Picture the person ‎you love the most in the world,

477
37:30.519 --> 37:34.899
‎and imagine you're expressing ‎your deep love to them.

478
37:35.858 --> 37:36.776
‎Now then.

479
37:38.736 --> 37:40.029
‎Again, from the top.

480
39:26.469 --> 39:30.389
‎NFCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE ‎KANG JI-HYE

481
39:33.100 --> 39:34.268
‎What is it?

482
39:34.351 --> 39:35.186
‎Hi.

483
39:36.187 --> 39:37.438
‎Ji-hye.

484
39:37.521 --> 39:40.357
‎Did you know your father is retiring?

485
39:41.358 --> 39:42.485
‎Retire?

486
39:42.568 --> 39:43.652
‎Your father

487
39:44.487 --> 39:47.323
‎is passing the baton to Jeong-yo ‎after the 80th anniversary performance

488
39:47.406 --> 39:48.699
‎and then retiring.

489
39:48.782 --> 39:50.951
‎Where is this coming from?

490
39:52.119 --> 39:54.163
‎Do you think he's unwell?

491
39:54.663 --> 39:57.374
‎He's passing the baton to Choi Jeong-yo?

492
40:00.127 --> 40:01.128
‎Father.

493
40:02.296 --> 40:05.591
‎There's no retirement age for a conductor, ‎so why are you stepping down?

494
40:05.674 --> 40:07.384
‎Who told you that?

495
40:08.594 --> 40:10.471
‎It was supposed to be a secret.

496
40:10.554 --> 40:11.889
‎Why is Choi Jeong-yo your successor?

497
40:11.972 --> 40:15.518
‎There are so many conductors ‎hoping to succeed you.

498
40:16.018 --> 40:18.437
‎Why would you pass it on ‎to someone so inexperienced?

499
40:18.521 --> 40:19.980
‎What's the matter with you?

500
40:21.440 --> 40:23.567
‎Why do you hate Choi Jeong-yo so much?

501
40:23.651 --> 40:25.694
‎Does he have something on you?

502
40:27.363 --> 40:28.864
‎Be kind.

503
40:30.366 --> 40:32.201
‎Or else you'll make more enemies,

504
40:32.284 --> 40:34.954
‎and your child will end up with bad karma.

505
40:35.037 --> 40:37.331
‎Do you still not know how the world works?

506
40:48.926 --> 40:50.052
‎Sorry to keep you waiting.

507
40:50.970 --> 40:51.804
‎I'm sorry.

508
40:52.721 --> 40:54.932
‎Mr. Kang, did you get some practice in?

509
40:56.100 --> 40:57.142
‎Let's hear you play.

510
42:08.505 --> 42:09.673
‎So?

511
42:12.551 --> 42:13.594
‎You didn't like it?

512
42:18.182 --> 42:20.476
‎Maybe my expectations were too high.

513
42:20.976 --> 42:23.145
‎Or maybe you needed more time ‎to study the score.

514
42:23.228 --> 42:26.482
‎Your interpretation ‎sounded too superficial.

515
42:27.066 --> 42:30.653
‎I can't even give you feedback ‎at this point.

516
42:31.362 --> 42:34.198
‎Why don't you study it some more ‎and try again next week?

517
42:34.948 --> 42:35.783
‎Thank you.

518
42:40.829 --> 42:43.499
‎What exactly didn't you like?

519
42:43.582 --> 42:46.794
‎I did my best to interpret it ‎and practiced just as hard.

520
42:48.295 --> 42:51.757
‎But if I'm going in the wrong direction, ‎you should tell me why.

521
42:52.758 --> 42:53.759
‎Oh…

522
42:55.177 --> 42:57.179
‎So this is what you call trying hard?

523
42:58.347 --> 43:01.266
‎Shall we go over everything ‎from the start then?

524
43:03.477 --> 43:05.771
‎Mr. Kang, what is the theme of this piece?

525
43:08.857 --> 43:11.443
‎The consequences ‎brought upon the arrogant.

526
43:13.320 --> 43:15.114
‎That's a convincing interpretation.

527
43:15.823 --> 43:19.993
‎Then why did you play ‎every phrase so beautifully?

528
43:20.703 --> 43:22.955
‎With all your experience,

529
43:23.038 --> 43:26.834
‎why are you still hiding ‎behind that armor?

530
43:29.753 --> 43:30.587
‎I'll see you next week.

531
43:33.340 --> 43:34.425
‎Good work today.

532
43:34.508 --> 43:35.551
‎Sorry about this.

533
43:40.889 --> 43:44.685
‎So are you going to ‎take the structure completely apart?

534
43:46.437 --> 43:48.063
‎-Yes. ‎-That's a great idea.

535
43:49.356 --> 43:51.358
‎A strong foundation ‎leads to better performance.

536
43:57.990 --> 43:58.824
‎Come in.

537
44:01.034 --> 44:01.952
‎It's a harpsichord.

538
44:19.011 --> 44:20.888
‎Can I practice on it for a few days?

539
44:20.971 --> 44:22.306
‎Of course.

540
44:22.389 --> 44:23.807
‎Thank you.

541
44:25.893 --> 44:26.935
‎Pi-o.

542
44:30.355 --> 44:31.356
‎Never mind.

543
44:31.440 --> 44:33.192
‎Just let me know when you leave.

544
44:35.569 --> 44:36.612
‎I will.

545
44:57.633 --> 44:59.843
‎Mr. Kang, what is the theme of this piece?

546
45:00.344 --> 45:03.013
‎The consequences ‎brought upon the arrogant.

547
45:03.096 --> 45:07.267
‎Then why did you play ‎every phrase so beautifully?

548
45:13.440 --> 45:15.859
‎With all your experience,

549
45:15.943 --> 45:19.738
‎why are you still hiding ‎behind that armor?

550
46:19.506 --> 46:20.507
‎What do you think?

551
46:22.092 --> 46:24.011
‎Does it still sound superficial?

552
46:24.886 --> 46:25.721
‎No.

553
46:26.388 --> 46:27.389
‎I love it.

554
46:27.472 --> 46:30.851
‎It's more than that. It's really moving.

555
46:31.977 --> 46:34.062
‎This is why I like you.

556
46:34.146 --> 46:36.356
‎I really think you're a genius.

557
46:37.733 --> 46:39.651
‎No need to flatter me so much.

558
46:39.735 --> 46:41.069
‎Come on, I'm serious.

559
46:42.279 --> 46:45.240
‎I read the score before hearing you play, ‎and there's no disconnect.

560
46:45.324 --> 46:46.241
‎Really?

561
47:34.247 --> 47:35.374
‎What do you think?

562
47:36.750 --> 47:38.543
‎Let's hear the cadenza again.

563
47:55.268 --> 47:56.186
‎Too slow.

564
48:00.148 --> 48:01.316
‎Too fast.

565
48:03.819 --> 48:04.653
‎It's slow.

566
48:09.741 --> 48:11.368
‎No, it's too fast!

567
48:13.704 --> 48:15.414
‎What do you think you're doing?

568
48:15.497 --> 48:17.124
‎How unprepared are you

569
48:17.207 --> 48:19.209
‎if you can't even ‎stay with the beat in the score?

570
48:19.292 --> 48:21.670
‎This is not the tempo I wanted.

571
48:23.588 --> 48:24.715
‎Try again and come back.

572
48:36.143 --> 48:37.018
‎Hey, Choi Jeong-yo.

573
48:40.814 --> 48:42.399
‎Explain it so that it makes sense.

574
48:44.651 --> 48:46.486
‎Here. This is 160.

575
48:47.070 --> 48:48.739
‎This is the tempo you wrote down.

576
48:48.822 --> 48:51.158
‎I practiced note by note to it.

577
48:51.241 --> 48:52.284
‎But you say I got it wrong?

578
48:52.784 --> 48:54.703
‎Which part did I play wrong?

579
48:54.786 --> 48:57.080
‎What is the tempo inside your head?

580
48:57.164 --> 48:57.998
‎Unbelievable.

581
48:59.916 --> 49:03.503
‎Why haven't you changed at all, Mr. Kang?

582
49:04.254 --> 49:05.422
‎Music is

583
49:07.007 --> 49:11.720
‎not a ready-made meal ‎you just heat up in the microwave.

584
49:11.803 --> 49:12.929
‎I'm begging you.

585
49:13.013 --> 49:15.140
‎Please feel the rhythm with your soul.

586
49:16.808 --> 49:20.437
‎How do you expect to fight and win ‎against a hundred orchestra members?

587
49:21.605 --> 49:22.647
‎Jeez.

588
49:32.657 --> 49:33.909
‎I don't get it.

589
49:35.160 --> 49:38.455
‎It sounded amazing to me.

590
49:39.456 --> 49:41.500
‎What was Jeong-yo not happy about?

591
49:42.751 --> 49:45.337
‎Do you want me to talk to him?

592
49:46.379 --> 49:47.297
‎No.

593
49:48.256 --> 49:50.842
‎I must've missed the composer's intent.

594
49:50.926 --> 49:52.427
‎I'll give it some more thought.

595
50:06.149 --> 50:07.192
‎Hey, what is it?

596
50:07.275 --> 50:08.527
‎There's a problem.

597
50:09.027 --> 50:11.863
‎Your dad disappeared, ‎and they haven't found him yet.

598
50:11.947 --> 50:12.823
‎What?

599
50:14.032 --> 50:15.200
‎When did he leave?

600
50:15.283 --> 50:16.368
‎I don't know.

601
50:16.451 --> 50:19.037
‎He went for a walk after lunch ‎and vanished.

602
50:19.120 --> 50:20.247
‎They only just found out?

603
50:21.164 --> 50:22.582
‎Just wait. I'll be right there.

604
50:51.528 --> 50:53.154
‎Did they check all the local bars?

605
50:53.238 --> 50:55.907
‎Yeah, they searched everywhere, ‎but he's nowhere to be found.

606
50:56.867 --> 50:58.869
‎They're asking whether ‎they should report him missing.

607
50:58.952 --> 51:00.203
‎Should we let them?

608
51:00.287 --> 51:01.580
‎Just wait a bit.

609
51:02.664 --> 51:04.124
‎Let me go check out the situation.

610
51:32.903 --> 51:36.156
‎ALCOHOL REHAB CENTER

611
52:00.221 --> 52:01.723
‎What brings you here, Ms. Kang?

612
52:04.100 --> 52:06.019
‎Oh, Jeong-yo.

613
52:07.062 --> 52:08.563
‎Why are you here?

614
52:09.189 --> 52:13.401
‎The director here asked me ‎if I could perform for the patients.

615
52:14.110 --> 52:16.154
‎But why are you here, Ms. Kang?

616
52:16.237 --> 52:17.155
‎Oh, I…

617
52:18.198 --> 52:20.325
‎I know someone who's a patient here,

618
52:20.408 --> 52:21.826
‎so I came to visit them.

619
52:21.910 --> 52:23.745
‎At an alcohol rehab center?

620
52:25.330 --> 52:26.164
‎Yes.

621
52:26.915 --> 52:30.085
‎It's amazing that you volunteer ‎despite your busy schedule.

622
52:32.128 --> 52:33.129
‎It's nothing.

623
52:34.130 --> 52:37.550
‎I'll need to hear the details ‎before I decide whether I can do it.

624
52:37.634 --> 52:38.593
‎Nothing's confirmed yet.

625
52:39.177 --> 52:40.178
‎I see.

626
52:40.261 --> 52:41.471
‎Still, it's amazing.

627
52:42.305 --> 52:44.849
‎I should get going. See you later.

628
52:45.433 --> 52:46.476
‎Goodbye.

629
52:58.405 --> 53:00.365
‎What's going on? Is she onto us?

630
53:03.118 --> 53:04.911
‎Did you tell the staff to keep quiet?

631
53:04.995 --> 53:07.872
‎They won't say a word. Don't worry.

632
53:09.666 --> 53:12.252
‎But seriously, where did your dad go?

633
53:14.337 --> 53:15.547
‎MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

634
53:15.630 --> 53:17.590
‎Hey, I don't think he's here.

635
53:18.633 --> 53:20.844
‎Let's call the cops ‎and report him missing.

636
53:22.429 --> 53:23.888
‎Where the hell is he?

637
53:25.432 --> 53:26.307
‎Hold on.

638
53:27.934 --> 53:28.768
‎What is it?

639
53:30.145 --> 53:33.231
‎KIM'S BOILED PORK

640
53:35.358 --> 53:36.943
‎Is there a reason we're here?

641
53:38.528 --> 53:39.487
‎What the heck?

642
53:41.448 --> 53:42.782
‎How did you know he'd be here?

643
53:43.825 --> 53:45.410
‎Look at him, all carefree.

644
53:54.419 --> 53:56.796
‎-Mr. Choi, do you recognize me? ‎-Huh?

645
53:56.880 --> 53:58.840
‎-What do you want? ‎-Let's get you back to the hospital.

646
53:58.923 --> 54:01.342
‎No, I'm not going back to the hospital.

647
54:01.426 --> 54:03.011
‎You need to go. You're a patient!

648
54:03.094 --> 54:05.013
‎-No, I don't want to. ‎-Come on, let's go!

649
54:05.096 --> 54:06.681
‎I'm not going!

650
54:08.725 --> 54:11.853
‎-No, I don't want to go back. ‎-Hey, don't run off!

651
54:11.936 --> 54:14.439
‎-I said I'm not going back there. ‎-It's this way, man.

652
54:15.148 --> 54:17.692
‎Who's been paying my hospital bills?

653
54:18.526 --> 54:20.361
‎Stop messing around ‎and stay put, will you?

654
54:20.445 --> 54:22.322
‎-I said I'm not going back! ‎-In you go.

655
54:26.910 --> 54:27.869
‎Go home.

656
55:00.026 --> 55:01.152
‎Music is

657
55:02.737 --> 55:07.492
‎not a ready-made meal ‎you just heat up in the microwave.

658
55:07.575 --> 55:08.660
‎I'm begging you.

659
55:08.743 --> 55:10.787
‎Please feel the rhythm with your soul.

660
56:08.803 --> 56:09.762
‎What are you doing here?

661
56:10.972 --> 56:11.806
‎Pi-o.

662
56:14.893 --> 56:18.271
‎What if Choi Jeong-yo ‎doesn't have amnesia?

663
56:18.354 --> 56:19.522
‎Just stop already.

664
56:20.773 --> 56:22.734
‎Do you still want to ‎shift the blame to him?

665
56:36.414 --> 56:37.916
‎That's not it, Pi-o.

666
56:37.999 --> 56:39.792
‎Something's strange about him.

667
56:40.835 --> 56:42.545
‎He has amnesia but returned to Korea.

668
56:42.629 --> 56:45.173
‎Out of all the orchestras, ‎he chose the Hankook Symphony.

669
56:45.256 --> 56:46.341
‎But most of all,

670
56:47.050 --> 56:48.801
‎he keeps getting involved with you.

671
56:50.178 --> 56:51.679
‎Isn't that strange?

672
56:53.556 --> 56:55.475
‎I just couldn't figure him out,

673
56:55.558 --> 56:57.560
‎so I followed him last night.

674
56:57.644 --> 57:01.356
‎And I saw him go inside ‎an alcohol rehab center.

675
57:04.400 --> 57:05.693
‎You followed him?

676
57:08.321 --> 57:09.572
‎Just listen for a second.

677
57:10.531 --> 57:12.367
‎He somehow found out I was following him

678
57:12.450 --> 57:14.077
‎and suddenly showed up acting friendly.

679
57:15.328 --> 57:17.622
‎He doesn't know a single person in Korea,

680
57:17.705 --> 57:20.583
‎yet he went to the outskirts of Seoul ‎to do volunteer work.

681
57:20.667 --> 57:22.502
‎It makes no sense when he's so busy.

682
57:23.878 --> 57:25.380
‎It was weird how he blocked me.

683
57:26.130 --> 57:27.507
‎He's hiding something.

684
57:27.590 --> 57:31.135
‎He had a strange look in his eyes ‎when I saw him at the Seodam Art Center.

685
57:32.053 --> 57:34.639
‎He left in the middle of the event, ‎went into a practice room,

686
57:34.722 --> 57:36.599
‎and stared out the window ‎through the curtains.

687
57:36.683 --> 57:37.517
‎Jeong-yo.

688
57:38.393 --> 57:40.311
‎He seemed very flustered when I walked in.

689
57:40.395 --> 57:41.396
‎Could it be

690
57:42.355 --> 57:43.898
‎that his memory is back?

691
57:44.941 --> 57:47.277
‎His mom passed away ‎at the Seodam Art Center.

692
57:48.695 --> 57:50.488
‎There's no way he could forget that.

693
57:53.032 --> 57:53.950
‎Mom.

694
57:54.450 --> 57:56.160
‎Stop wasting your time imagining things.

695
57:56.744 --> 57:57.954
‎And stop following Jeong-yo.

696
57:59.289 --> 58:00.498
‎If you do that again…

697
58:02.667 --> 58:04.252
‎I won't let it slide.

698
58:25.064 --> 58:28.318
‎Why haven't you changed at all, Mr. Kang?

699
58:36.909 --> 58:40.496
‎How do you expect to fight and win ‎against a hundred orchestra members?

700
58:40.580 --> 58:42.248
‎So in a concerto,

701
58:42.332 --> 58:45.668
‎a pianist has to fight and win ‎against a hundred orchestra members,

702
58:46.294 --> 58:47.879
‎while still working together at times.

703
58:48.504 --> 58:50.465
‎Avoiding a slump

704
58:50.548 --> 58:52.425
‎isn't going to solve anything.

705
58:52.508 --> 58:55.470
‎You need to face it at some point.

706
58:55.553 --> 58:58.014
‎Ignoring the problem won't solve anything.

707
58:59.015 --> 59:01.434
‎You need to face it at some point.

708
59:26.250 --> 59:27.877
‎He's hiding something.

709
59:27.960 --> 59:31.422
‎He had a strange look in his eyes ‎when I saw him at the Seodam Art Center.

710
59:40.807 --> 59:44.185
‎What if Choi Jeong-yo ‎doesn't have amnesia?

711
59:56.572 --> 59:58.574
‎Pi-o, let's make a promise.

712
59:59.158 --> 01:00:00.952
‎Let's play some more four hands

713
01:00:01.035 --> 01:00:03.079
‎even after the competition.

714
01:00:03.162 --> 01:00:03.996
‎Okay.

715
01:00:16.968 --> 01:00:19.846
‎He left in the middle of the event, ‎went into a practice room,

716
01:00:19.929 --> 01:00:21.681
‎and stared out the window ‎through the curtains.

717
01:00:27.478 --> 01:00:29.105
‎He seemed very flustered when I walked in.

718
01:00:29.188 --> 01:00:30.022
‎Could it be

719
01:00:31.315 --> 01:00:32.859
‎that his memory is back?

720
01:00:43.035 --> 01:00:45.455
‎Promise you won't sulk ‎if I win first place.

721
01:00:45.538 --> 01:00:46.956
‎Let's still have fun when we hang out.

722
01:00:47.039 --> 01:00:49.041
‎But I'm going to win first place.

723
01:00:49.125 --> 01:00:49.959
‎Don't get sulky yourself.

724
01:00:55.465 --> 01:00:58.259
‎SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK ‎FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

725
01:01:18.780 --> 01:01:20.907
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

726
01:01:20.990 --> 01:01:22.700
‎I know you remember everything.

727
01:01:22.784 --> 01:01:24.744
‎Why did you tell such a lie?

728
01:01:25.536 --> 01:01:28.623
‎I don't understand what you're saying.

729
01:01:28.706 --> 01:01:31.793
‎We need to get rid of him ‎so he can't talk.

730
01:01:31.876 --> 01:01:33.085
‎Just call me Kim.

731
01:01:33.669 --> 01:01:36.964
‎I didn't struggle to come back alive ‎just to give you a free pass.

732
01:01:37.048 --> 01:01:38.132
‎And here!

733
01:01:38.883 --> 01:01:42.053
‎At this rate, both of you will go down.

734
01:01:42.136 --> 01:01:43.930
‎Whether I ruin my fingers ‎or the performance,

735
01:01:44.013 --> 01:01:45.389
‎I'll take full responsibility.

736
01:01:46.432 --> 01:01:47.892
‎Break the mold, Pi-o.

737
01:01:49.435 --> 01:01:54.440
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
